      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Number 18 Oldtown Walk is a stunning family home, spanning approximately 181 sq. m. (1,947 sq. ft.) and located in the exclusive Oldtown Walk development, just minutes from Naas, Co. Kildare. Built in 2018 by Westin Homes, this elegant 3-storey detached residence presents in immaculate condition with high-quality finishes and a beautifully landscaped, south-facing rear garden.\r\n\r\nOriginally a 5-bedroom home, the property has been tastefully reconfigured into a spacious 4-bedroom layout. At ground level, the home features a modern kitchen diner with integrated appliances, feature lighting, and a walk-in larder. The sitting room is warm and inviting, with a bay window and a stunning Wanders Lenge 800 gas fire. A utility room with a sink and a separate wc complete the downstairs accommodation.\r\n\r\nThe first-floor master bedroom has been enlarged, offering a luxurious ensuite with a large shower and Bluetooth-enabled bathroom cabinet. Two additional double bedrooms, one currently used as a home office, complete the first floor alongside a family bathroom with a separate bath and shower.\r\n\r\nThe second floor boasts another bright master suite with fitted wardrobes and ensuite, along with a shelved hot press.\r\n\r\nSet in a small development of just 50 homes, the property also benefits from a large driveway and a Steeltech shed. Solar panels provide eco-friendly water heating.\r\n\r\nArea Info:\r\n\r\nBounded by the walls of the original Oldtown Demesne and with an abundance of mature trees and open spaces, this truly is an enviable place to live. Oldtown Walk is just a stroll to local schools, parkland, GAA, Grand Canal walks and Monread shopping centre. The vibrant of town of Naas offers many restaurants, bars, theatre and leisure facilities, all within walking distance. For the commuter, it is a 4 minute' drive to the M7/N7 motorway, a 20 minute drive to the Luas in Citywest and the Arrow rail link in Sallins is either a 4 minute drive or a 20 minute walk away.\r\n\r\nThe nearest bus stop is just a 5 minute walk from the property and is serviced by the 139 & 821 providing regular routes to to Blanchardstown & Newbridge.\r\n\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: Any intending purchaser(s) shall accept that no statement, description or measurement contained in advertisement or any other document or published by the vendor or by Moovingo, in respect of the premises shall constitute a representation inducing the purchaser(s) to enter into any contract for sale, or any warranty forming part of any such contract for sale. Any such statement, description or measurement, whether in writing or in oral form, given by the vendor, or by Moovingo, are for illustration purposes only and are not to be taken as matters of fact. Any intending purchaser(s) shall satisfy themselves by inspection, survey or otherwise as to the correctness of same. No omission, misstatement, misdescription, incorrect measurement or error of any description, whether given orally or in any written form by the vendor or by Moovingo, shall give rise to any claim for compensation against the vendor or against Moovingo. Any intending purchaser(s) are deemed to fully satisfy themselves in relation to all such matters."
